Hello all! Just out of curiosity, I compared the shape of some structures before and after carrying out a Generalized Procrustes Analysis (made with gpagen), and I realized that there are some slight differences. The differences are small, but considering that (as far as I understand it), gpa only rotates, translates and resizes shapes, I am a bit worried that these aberrations are not normal, perhaps an artifact of the sort of analysis I am doing. These aberrations appear in landmarks that vary considerably in position between different taxa, while landmarks that are somewhat relatively stable position-wise do not display these aberrations post-gpa.
Any help in this matter would be really appreciated.

