Vincente,

Are you using any sliding semilandmarks? These of course will move before/after GPA, which can result in the appearance of other movements relative to their positions. Otherwise, they will not do what you are claiming: it is not mathematically possible.

Also, it is not clear when you mentioned you were worried that these may be an ‘artifact of the sort of analysis I am doing’. It is challenging to confirm that a standard method (such as GPA) is doing what intended if the user is not using it in the manner in which it should be used.

Dean

