Jayme,

Please have a careful look at the help file for both procD.lm and pairwise.

Your procedure and pipeline are generally correct: first run a full factorial model, and then run pairwise comparisons on the set of components you wish to investigate. However, the latter component may require a bit more thinking, as one could (and sometimes should) include the covariate in those cases. Your data suggest that is the case, as the overall covariate/regression term is highly significant, displays a very large effect size, and thus influences patterns in your data.

Thus, pairwise for your case should include that covariate, as per your second example. Finally, note that changing the test statistic in that function will test for the length of vectors, their direction=slopes, or disparity=variance. A careful reading of the help files will provide additional guidance.

Best,

Dean

